From be2a44e766cad2217083eea177cf3098f18b8bae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TherryHilaire <therryhilaire@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 11:05:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] egis0576: Add driver for EgisTec EH576 (1c7a:0576)

Add support for the EgisTec EH576 image sensor found in e.g. the
Lenovo IdeaPad Flex 5 16ABR8 (82XY).

The driver is based on the fp-eh0576 reverse engineering effort by
Marcel (Sprayxe) and Animeshz's EH575 work, with these changes
verified live against bcdDevice 15.72:

- Response layout is SIGE REG VALUE STATUS [data...]; responses do
  NOT echo the command byte. The poll check (buffer[6] & 0x01) tests
  the STATUS byte, which is always 0x01 - it is kept only to mirror
  the Windows driver flow and is not a finger-detect condition.
- Finger presence cannot be read from registers; it is decided from
  image content (variance / dark portion heuristic).
- Captures are quality gated: frames yielding fewer than 10 NBIS
  minutiae are rejected as partial/blurred presses instead of being
  added to the template. This fixes most flaky-matching reports.
- Contrast normalization stretches the difference histogram between
  its 2nd/98th percentile rather than absolute extremes, raising
  within-region bozorth scores by ~78% on a 35-frame dataset.
---
